This directory vendors the LIBERO benchmark simulator and its assets.

LIBERO — Liu et al., "LIBERO: Benchmarking Knowledge Transfer for Lifelong Robot
Learning" (NeurIPS 2023). Released under the MIT License.
Upstream: https://github.com/Lifelong-Robot-Learning/LIBERO

The simulator is built on robosuite (MIT License,
https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robosuite) and MuJoCo.

Modifications by the CANON authors: the agent-view camera in
`envs/problems/libero_tabletop_manipulation.py` was made a perturbable spherical
camera (azimuth = view angle, fixed elevation/lookat, varying distance) to render
the multi-view pretraining pool and the viewpoint-perturbed evaluation cameras.
The 3D assets, BDDL task files, and init files under `assets/`, `bddl_files/`, and
`init_files/` are redistributed unmodified from LIBERO. Please retain this notice
and respect the upstream MIT licenses.

`assets/` (410MB of meshes/textures) is not stored in this git repo; download it
from the companion HF dataset and place it here:

    huggingface-cli download agentic-learning-ai-lab/canonical \
        --repo-type dataset --include "libero_sim_assets/*" \
        --local-dir /tmp/libero_sim_assets
    mv /tmp/libero_sim_assets/libero_sim_assets libero_goal/envs/assets

(run from the repo root; `libero_goal/envs/assets/` must exist with this exact
name for the simulator to find it)
